    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0491" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v02/pg461"/>

                <head>261. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Mission at the United Nations<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d261-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-12-19T21:06:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                                1960—9:06 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1188. Re Mauritanian Membership.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>USGADel should endeavor persuade sponsors 11-power draft<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d261-f2"/> agree postpone consideration their resolution until
                        resumed session on grounds Soviet amendments raise highly controversial
                        Outer Mongolian issue and consideration this issue now could result in
                        either postponement recess date or failure complete more pressing questions
                        prior recess. If unsuccessful this effort, USGADel should support 11-power
                        draft resolution reported urtel
                        1807.</item>
                    <pb facs="0492" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>As proposed reftel USGADel should
                        strongly oppose any amendment to include Outer Mongolia this draft
                        resolution and also oppose consideration as separate resolution Outer
                        Mongolia and other pending applications at this time. Del should actively seek support other friendly
                            dels for this purpose.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>If draft resolution amended to include Outer Mongolia, delegation should
                        abstain on amended resolution.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>USGADel should endeavor persuade sponsors 11-power draft substitute
                        “finding” for “decision” in operative paragraph 2 draft resolution since
                            GA cannot make decisions.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>USGADel should make no statements or explanations of vote.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d261-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d261-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 303/12–1860. Confidential; Priority.
                    Drafted by Hartley, initialed by
                        Cargo, cleared with FE and in substance with Monsma, and approved by Sisco who signed for Herter.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d261-f2" n="2" xml:id="d261-f2-content">
                <p>Reference is to a draft resolution favoring Mauritania’s admission to the United
                    Nations, submitted to the U.N. General Assembly
                    by 11 African nations. Its text was transmitted to the Department in telegram
                    1807 from USUN, December 18. (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid</hi>.) For text, see U.N. doc. A/L.335.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
